ity boom  in international markets as a result  Brazil became the seventh largest  economy in the world in 2010 practically  tied with the six largest as you can see  here however it has since Fallen to 12th  Place in this recent ranking  when the oil Bonanza came to an end  things started to fall apart what's more  deliver Rusev's government was Lethal  for the Brazilian economy and it went  into a deep recession even the country's  largest company the state-owned oil  giant petrobras was on the ropes and  close to bankruptcy people's discontent  propelled one of the most controversial  political figures in recent years where  of course talking about jair bolsonaro  his populist discourse captivated  millions of Brazilians who were tired of  the numerous corruption scandals that  played the workers party after 16 years  of government however one of President  bolsonaro's greatest successes was to  incorporate Paulo guadus as a sort of  super Minister for economic affairs  [Music]  Paulo holds a PhD in economics from the  University of Chicago a model  Institution for economic liberalism  since he became Minister he has promoted  an agenda focused on promoting  privatization simplifying labor  regulations and reducing bureaucracy an  impossible mission from the outset since  according to World Bank data Brazil has  one of the most complex and inefficient  tax legislations in the world  specifically it ranks 184th in the world  banked ranking of 190 tax systems  [Music]  the labor reform promoted by The  bolsonaro guader's Duo has had good  results Brazil's unemployment rate has  reached 12 percent when both came to  power currently and despite the  coronavirus this has been reduced to  below nine percent the lowest figure  since 2015. another card played by  greatest was to bet on privatizations to  reduce public debt  to convince Brazilians bolsonaro has had  it easy but of course it was not  complicated to improve on the economic  management of his predecessors  foreign  however this desire to reduce the size  of the state Machinery came up against  reality it is true that it carried out  the largest privatization in two decades  but in the end it did not dare with the  petrobrass oil company so basically  everything was limited to a partial  privatization of electrobras the  state-owned company in charge of  electricity generation in the country a  privatization that attracted investment  from the Singapore Sovereign wealth fund  and the Canadian pension fund it also  allowed private investment in water and  sewage be that as it may the important  thing is that between one thing and  another the results came in  [Music]  the best news for Brazil is that after a  decade of weak economic growth the  Country Returns to reasonably good  numbers at least considering that we are  talking about Brazil a terribly  bureaucratic and unfriendly economy for  business even by Latin American  Standards well the pandemic drank Brazil  down by four percent in 2020 but in 2021  GDP grew by 4.6 and in 2022 at the time  of the elections year-on-year growth was  still above 3 these positive data and a  tremendously polarized discourse helps  to form a community of true Fanatics  around the president bolsonarismo  foreign  wait a minute it wasn't also Rosy  because the numbers are reasonably good  yes the truth is that the economy has  grown in large part thanks to the  government's stimulus policies  [Music]  in view of the polls bolsonaro set aside  economic theory and pulled out all his  artillery to achieve a comeback he  approved an aid program with lower taxes  on fuel electricity gas and public  transportation he also bet on improving  social benefits the excuse as you can  imagine inflation the motive as you can  also well imagine was to give a little  gift to the voters don't forget that for  politicians poor Brazilians have only  one thing that as much value as that of  the rich their vote so to achieve this  goal bolsonaro launched into extending  and even expanding the social measures  he put in place during the pandemic  bolsonaro raises axillil Brazil from 400  to 600 it was undoubtedly his star  measure we're talking about the fact  that this 50 increase brought auxilo  Brazil to about a hundred and ten  dollars per month  foreign  after the first round of Elections he  promised to extend this Aid during 2023.  the bill for this all is no joke right  now orcillo Brazil is being received by  21 million Brazilian families so  currency up currency down bolsonaro  committed Aid worth over 50 billion  dollars including new debt forgiveness  programs and lines of credit however  visual politic viewers all this was not  enough for bolsonaro he had many wrongs  to write and the election campaign  against Lula was like putting palmyra's  fans together with Corinthians fans  listen up  [Music]  The Two Towers  [Music]  Bolson arrows Administration has had  significant downsides denying the  importance of covid-19 made Brazil the  country with the second highest number  of deaths from coronavirus in the world  with almost 700 000 deaths downplaying  the importance of the upturn in Amazon  logging does not seem to be the best  move in an international scene dominated  by environmental concerns either and  arguing for an outdated concept of the  role of women in modern societies  creates an obstacle that a good part of  the electorate can't get past in order  to vote for you even so he almost  managed to win re-election in a  confrontation between the two most  important figures in Brazilian politics  so far this Century because Lula also  generates rejection from certain groups  [Music]  former president Lula de Silva was  imprisoned after being charged with  corruption in the lava Jato Scandal  surrounding the state-owned oil company  petrovas he spent 19 months in prison  before being released by the Supreme  Court which annulled all sentences  against Lula on the grounds that the  matter was beyond 