ustry and after a campaign without  clear proposals it seems that these  issues do not matter to any politician  nor to their voters among whom are the  fanatic masses whose only objective  seems to be to defeat their opponents  that's where it fits that there are  bolsonaro supporters begging the Army to  Stage a coup against Lula they seem to  be willing to do anything although not  as much as some would have us believe  Boston Arrow supporters use their phones  to call for an alien coup some  prestigious media have fallen into the  temptation of giving varissa militude to  this new story in order to ridicule  bolsonaro's supporters billions of  Brazilians would be delighted if E.T  could heal Neymar's ankle as if it were  Elliot's finger but visualpolitik  viewers as so often happens the reality  is much less interesting than the  headlines press released fake news about  protesters in Porto Alegre although Kim  in mind we are not talking about nothing  [Music]  those cell phone flashlights directed  towards the sky are one more  demonstration of Brazilian citizens  asking the Armed Forces yet again for a  coup d'etat not the aliens or to show  off an sosfa which could capture a drone  from the sky but not the Millennium  Falcon check it out despite all this it  seems that bolsonaro has accepted defeat  and is not going to mount a trump-style  Capitol Hill the bad news for Lula is  that he will still find it much more  difficult to run Brazil than the last  time he was in office the country is  more divided than it was then and its  public finances are in worse shape  however now is the time for Brazil to  tackle structural changes and move  towards a productive model that will lay  the foundations for long-term economic  growth so what will be Lulu's main  challenges we're about to take a look  [Music]  the return of Lula  Lula de Silva wants to put the state  back at the center of the Brazilian  economy to this end he plans to use  public spending to stimulate 