ity of public debt of  course with Congress against him this  does not appear to be a straightforward  task in any case the person lular  chooses as his minister of economy will  have a lot to say about this it seems  that he already has a name Lula is  leaning towards ex-mayor Haddad to helm  Brazil's economy Haddad is a choice from  the moderate left as mayor of Sao Paulo  between 2013 and 2016 he reduced the  budget deficit and secured for the city  and investment grade credit rating he's  not driven by populist policies and that  is good news for Brazil but now the  question is over to you do you think  that a president like Lula de Silva is  what Brazil needs or do you think  bolsonaro deserves a second term to  fully develop his policies you can leave  me your answer in the comments as always  if you found the video interesting  please like and don't forget to  subscribe to visualpolitik all the best  see you next time  [Music]


